Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 10:10:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06882/11362] [outer-loop] ARC lf52 round-5: L4->L5,
 torch-ferry logistics solved

Round-5 claude-fable-5 attempt on lf52 solved L5 after 3 prior codex
timeouts on this game, by directly executing round-3's own fix
recommendation: zero PNG-rendering tooling built, zero resets, zero
wasted jumps. L5's endgame is a torch-ferry logistics puzzle on a closed
rectangular rail network -- the single east-network carrier ferries one
movable torch, and parking it on a rail at a peg's row/column band
creates a temporary crossable obstacle between two socket cells. The win
is a global reduce-to-one plan: 5 pegs need 4 peg-over-peg removals, each
arranged so the jumper survives on a cell from which its next leg is
reachable. Confirmed the west and east rail networks are permanently
disconnected -- the endgame must use only the east carrier's torch plus
the 4 fixed hub torches.

Fresh-reset reproduce() gate confirmed reached_level=5. Independently
re-verified by the outer loop: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via a new
resolver priority branch, all 5 confirmed level=5, state=NOT_FINISHED.

L6 previewed (not attempted): a self-jumpable color-8 quad block, a
double-socket carrier. The prior L3-line artifact content is preserved
verbatim at a dated sibling file before this session overwrote it.

reproducible_total_levels 156 -> 157. arc_count_integrity_lint.py exit 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
